it's January 3rd 2019 so it's time for  another monthly update video in which  I'll talk about what we've got coming up  in January and what went on in December  I'll also be doing another sort of  end-of-the-year wrap up the year to come  video a little bit later this month it  might do a video premiere with that  we'll see I'll figure out exactly what  I'm doing and announce it later but  before that I always bring up three big  things for the month ahead and the  things that we've got going on are  pretty exciting this month big thing  number one I know I've promised this but  I will be bringing out some new  teachable classes some of them actually  free over the course of this month so  pay attention to my social media where  you'll see those listed as they appear  big thing number two we're moving into  year four believe it or not of the  worlds of speculative fiction series I  picked nine of the authors and I had my  fan subscribers readers viewers come up  with the other three so if you missed  the announcement about that I'll link to  the the blog post in or exes do you know  what to Kay about that maybe I'll shoot  a video about the series as well coming  up for the year and talked about it a  bit and of course there's the online  teachable class where you can see all  the videos and get the resources as well  big thing number three I'm beginning the  first preliminary work on a massive  editing project as many of you know I'm  the editor of Stoicism today and it's  about time that we brought out another  volume of Stoicism today selected essays  that is one of my big goals for the year  and it begins with this month with me  going through and laying some of the  groundwork for that so those are the  three big things let's talk now about  the month of December December was quite  a busy month for me but you might not  have suspected it by  looking at my online presence because I  didn't actually create and release all  that much content but it was because of  everything else that was going on I did  have a few events some of them online  some of them face-to-face here we had  the final worlds of speculative fiction  series talk of the year this time on  Jean wolf a living author had a great  time with that we've got the video for  that linked to below  I went on the skräuss is radio show  image for hire and we talked about doing  philosophy then we talked about HP  Lovecraft you can see the video for that  below and then of course there was the  monthly stoic fellowship and I was able  to take my son Matthew along to that he  has actually been studying a little bit  of epictetus so I thought it would be  good and he had a great time at the  fellowship then of course we had our  usual Hagel sessions and the pop ups and  the AMA asked me anything session you  can see videos for some of those linked  to below it was a very busy month in  terms of classes I taught five different  classes two of them online intensive you  know eight in seven week classes three  of them face to face I was teaching for  four different institutions so all of  that was coming to an end around the  middle two to three quarters mark of  December just before the holiday times  and it seemed like there was an  extraordinary amount of work involved as  various student issues and grading and  giving tests and students needing to  reschedule their exams at Marquette one  of my exams is actually scheduled for  the very last day the very last hour so  some of the students understandably  enough needed to reschedule that since  their parents had already made  arrangements for them to travel wherever  you know they were going some of them to  California some of them to Hawaii you  know the places that they came from so  there was a lot of student work involved  for different learning management  platforms you know I was working in  blackboard Sakai Moodle and d2l so that  was just on the course end then I had  all of my work with my clients doing  consulting philosophical counseling a  lot of tutorial work especially as the  semester comes to an end some academic  coaching and then there was my kids  arriving and and my kids didn't arrive  until after Christmas this year but then  they were here and you know I think I've  learned the lesson by now that when  they're here I probably shouldn't plan  on getting an awful lot done except  perhaps in the summer visitation so I  just kind of you know after I got the  grading stuff done Andy and I we took it  easy for about you know a week although  she was actually having to do a lot of  work on her end and then the kids  arrived and we had a great time with  them so you know a lot of activity and  you know getting to see some relatives  and friends as well I did get some work  done on writing I worked on that that  book project which focuses on how to  make end-of-life decisions well for  aging and ill pets I did some other  writing in in blogs particularly erectus  Deana wet DK and I got some content  worked up that I need to to start  working through I also did video work as  usual didn't do as much as I had  originally hoped I got three of the six  half-hour Haegele videos which is better  than the 2 and the 1 and the 0 of the  previous months but I'm still not up to  the full quota of 6 but hopefully that  is going to change and I shot some  Augustine core concept videos did videos  of course of the various events and so  all of those have been posted the  Augustine videos interestingly are  getting a lot of traction much more than  I thought they would have I guess a lot  of people have been waiting for that  content so that's what took place in the  south  and now let's talk about January this  month is going to be pretty busy but  it's going to be a lot of behind the  scenes sorts of things I do have quite a  few events lined up although not as much  as I do in in some other months of the  year we begin on the 8th at 5 p.m.  central standard time with Hegel Q&amp;A  that's public anybody can come if you  have an interest in German idealism or  in Hegel or in philosophy in general pop  in and join the conversation  then here locally at the Brookfield  public library on the 10th at 7:00 p.m.  we will kick off year four of the worlds  of speculative fiction series this time  talking about one of the great  grandfather's of horror and speculative  fiction Edgar Allan Poe so that's going  to be if you're in the area you don't  want to miss that we're gonna have a  great conversation  hopefully we'll actually have enough  room for all the attendees because they  think that one's going to be a big draw  on the 12th at 12 p.m. Central Standard  Time online event I'll have my ask me  anything session open to anybody to ask  me whatever they want usually I planned  them for an hour and we usually go an  hour and a half and there's still  questions left over then on the 19th  about a week from then at 3 p.m.  we'll have our philosophy chat for  patreon supporters and finally finishing  up on the 31st the very last Thursday of  the month at 6 p.m. at the Shorewood  Public Library we will have our MKE that  is Milwaukee stoic fellowship meeting  we're currently working through  Epictetus discourses so if you have an  interest in stoicism you don't have to  be particularly well-versed in it it's a  place for learning just pop in and we're  happy to to have you and to discuss the  the works with you  classes are beginning  this coming week but the week after that  and I have five more classes this  semester I have to with Marquette  University - with Milwaukee Institute of  Art and Design and one with Milwaukee  Area Technical College I'm very  fortunate in that all of these are  within about a miles walk of where I  live here in Milwaukee but I am going to  be one busy guy because that's more than  a full-time load you might say well why  did you take on so many classes well  because I got a lot of requests for  teaching and you know I people you know  the students really like the classes  that I offer and I do enjoy the  face-to-face teaching so I decided to  take on this much and you know we'll see  how it goes  fortunately all but one of these classes  are courses that I've taught a number of  times before and the the one outlier is  a really cool class for the Milwaukee  Institute of Art Design ethics for  artists and designers and maybe I'll  actually do a video about that once I  get the reading list put up in the  curriculum because that's that's a  really cool applied ethics class so I'm  I'm looking forward to that and hanging  out with my students and seeing where  they're coming from and getting to to  chat and building the course sites and  that's a lot of work then I of course  have my client work through reason I oh  I'm doing consulting doing academic  coaching tutorials I've got a few new  clients beginning with me and some  philosophical counseling as well so that  will keep me quite busy there's a lot of  planning going going on right now behind  the scenes for what we're going to be  doing I want to get to some of my  academic writing projects and some  popular writing as well and like I  pointed out I will be doing some editing  work not just the regular stuff or  stoicism today which is already kind of  a big commitment but to try to bring out  a new volume of selected essays from  the previous two two and a half years of  Stoicism  today I'll also be bringing out as I  pointed out earlier some new classes in  my teachable Academy  I've retitled it as study with dr.  Sadler so if you just type study with  dr. Sandler that should come up  otherwise I'll simply put the link below  for you so that's that's a lot of stuff  going on that's not even getting to the  videos which we should talk about now  all right you're watching one of them at  this moment as I mentioned I need to get  cracking on the half hour hagel videos  and want to get some more momentum going  get us up to six videos per month and  I've got to start shooting some new core  concept videos that I'm gonna be using  in my classes this semester so I just  finished shooting some videos earlier  today on Plato's allegory of the cave I  got to do some other Plato stuff on book  6 of the Republic and then I'm going to  get to the Arendt videos that I wanted  to do before on Eichmann in Jerusalem  there's Augustine videos we're switching  to doing Augustine's on free choice of  the will so I need to do some videos on  that des cartes meditations I did videos  on des cartes discourses but now I need  to do some Monday cartes meditations and  so that's really the stuff that's on the  docket for this month I probably won't  be releasing all of it this month but I  will be shooting all of it this month  and if I get really ambitious I'll also  shoot some and some and Aquinas  materials as well I'm gonna shoot some  book review videos hopefully I'm gonna  get started on that this weekend and I  do have a few other Q&amp;A videos from  those old series that I was doing before  mostly about stoic philosophy I'll shoot  those this month and I might do a video  premiere we'll see how that works out if  I do a premiere you'll see it on my  Facebook page and I'll announce it in  other places as well I should mention  that there are other videos that my  patreon supporters get to see that not  everybody does I shoot these  slice-of-life videos  and I'll start doing those much more  frequently for my patreon supporters and  then there's also outtakes and bloopers  and things like that that they get to  see as well the last thing I should  mention podcasts I'm going to start you  know getting work done on the podcast  again the Sadler's lectures podcast it  was in the middle of podcast episodes on  epictetus discourses so i'm going to be  producing more of those I've got quite a  few lecture videos that need to be given  that treatment and then after that I'll  get on to some Aristotle material what  exactly I'm not quite sure I have to  think about what needs to get out first  I have you know over 150 Aristotle  videos so there's a lot of content to be  converted the last thing that I'll  mention is you know we are lining up  speaking opportunities and and and  engagements for the year to come if you  you're interested in having me come  speak send me an e-mail at Gregg at  reason IO and we'll talk about whether  it's it's feasible and how to make it  happen if you're interested in in  bringing me in you can either do so  yourself or suggest to a local  organization whatever it is a university  library Church let's bring this guy in  to talk and I'm game for for doing  travel it'll be a little bit of you know  trickiness if it's if it's very distant  from here given my teaching schedule but  you know we can always make it happen  so there's that check out the teachable  Academy check out the videos as I'm  releasing them and stay tuned for stuff  coming from stoicism today and from the  various blogs that I write for as well  as edit a lot of stuff lined up hope you  have a great month and hopefully I'll  see some of you at these events whether  online or face to face  you
 

